fastkeccak

This package descends from golang.org/x/crypto/sha3, which is where its
Keccak-256 semantics come from and which it still calls directly on platforms
and CPUs without an accelerated path.

Portions are derived from code copyright The Go Authors:

  * keccakf_arm64.s — the Keccak-f[1600] round body is taken verbatim from
    Go's src/crypto/internal/fips140/sha3/sha3_arm64.s. The file retains its
    original copyright header; the fused XOR-and-permute entry path and the
    frame declaration are the local additions.

